  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence of integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. You have to answer QQQ queries.\n\nIn each query, you are given two integers LLL and RRR, and you have to find the number of ordered pairs (X,Y)(X, Y)(X,Y) such that L≤X,Y≤RL \\le X, Y \\le RL≤X,Y≤R and AX≤AX⊕AY≤AYA_X \\le A_X \\oplus A_Y \\le A_YAX​≤AX​⊕AY​≤AY​. Here, ⊕\\oplus⊕ is the bitwise XOR operator.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤50,0001 \\le T \\le 50,0001≤T≤50,000",
      "1≤N,Q≤5⋅1051 \\le N, Q \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤5⋅105",
      "0≤Ai&lt;2300 \\le A_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​&lt;230 for each valid iii",
      "1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105",
      "the sum of QQQ over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains two space-separated integers LLL and RRR describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing one integer ― the number of valid pairs.",
